/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046647 #edb/ref 1008 "Mathematical Foundations II is the second course in a sequence specially crafted for adults seeking the most direct path to prepare for university math courses. Building on the basic algebra covered in Mathematical Foundations I , students in Mathematical Foundations II generalize their understanding of algebra to more advanced functions (including trigonometry) and become acquainted with limits and derivatives in calculus. Upon completing the course, students will be prepared for Mathematical Foundations III , the final stepping stone in preparing for university-level math." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046647 #edb/ref 1009 "Master the algebra of advanced functions including quadratics, logarithms, and trigonometry. Dive deep into the theory of polynomials, learn the basics of limits, derivatives, and integrals from calculus, and explore a variety of concepts from higher math including complex numbers, vectors, probability, and statistics." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046647 #edb/ref 1012 111 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046647 #edb/ref 1013 "MF2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046647 #edb/ref 1014 #uuid "b5d8b420-892a-5b6a-8150-ba3c70c4d779" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048906 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048906 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186073779 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048906 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186073781 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048906 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186073904 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048906 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186073905 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048906 #edb/ref 1031 "Combining Geometric Transformations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048906 #edb/ref 1033 483 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048906 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "cb5f4251-e56e-5612-a19a-b98c9b2d1546" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049020 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050231 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049020 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050239 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049020 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133853 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049020 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133971 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049020 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133972 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049020 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133974 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049020 #edb/ref 1031 "Stretches of Geometric Figures" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049020 #edb/ref 1033 2217 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049020 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "d4577aec-62a4-5b08-b9e4-6d82f0c922c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050239 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048906 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050239 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186105842 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050239 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186105843 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050239 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186105844 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050239 #edb/ref 1031 "Combining Stretches of Geometric Figures" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050239 #edb/ref 1033 1363 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050239 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "38b346ff-89c2-5572-8fdf-5d288e6ae126" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105352 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186105353 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105352 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186105355 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105352 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186534342 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105352 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186534421 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105352 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186534650 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105352 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105352 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105352 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186105353 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105352 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "af8b2139-6d53-5b18-926c-04ee1c2734e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105353 #edb/ref 1080 "(8,-6)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105353 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105353 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8ae5059f-bcf0-56ad-8d2b-a7753f3f2165" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105355 #edb/ref 1080 "(12,-4)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105355 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105355 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d7670310-6908-57ff-a1cc-003fdf97fe7d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105679 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7859" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105679 #edb/ref 1071 "The stretch $S(x,y) = \\left(\\dfrac{3}{2}x,2y\\right)$ is applied to the polygon shown below. Find the resulting polygon.\n\n![](images/a3/a36f0ee4e491e0518041f7e033392b9f16e12c4e2501e707d8328af78aa89efd.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105679 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "36445a36-7b68-5ba1-847e-7fd720138dd6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105679 #edb/ref 1074 "To stretch a polygon, we \n\n- find the images of the vertices, and then\n\n- draw segments connecting the image vertices.\n\nSo, our three vertices $(2,1)$, $(4,1)$, $(2,2)$ are mapped to the following points by the stretch:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2,1) & ↦(\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 2,\\,2\\cdot 1)=(3,2) \\\\ (4,1) & ↦(\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 4,\\,2\\cdot 1)=(6,2) \\\\ (2,2) & ↦(\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 2,\\,2\\cdot 2)=(3,4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following result:\n\n![](images/b9/b961a446536bddbe6ff529e7ca2973c8e957c185ef4d6f00b9255d09baa9d3cc.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105680 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7860" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105680 #edb/ref 1071 "What function represents the combined stretch of factor $4$ in the $x$-direction and factor $\\dfrac 1 4$ in the $y$-direction?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105680 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "228d023c-b74d-56a9-ab02-638594472f43" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105680 #edb/ref 1074 "- A stretch in the $x$-direction of factor $4$ can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\mapsto (4x,y).\n$$\n\n- A stretch in the $y$-direction of factor $\\dfrac 1 4$ can be represented by the function \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\mapsto \\left(x,\\dfrac 1 4y\\right).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the combination of the stretches is given by\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\mapsto \\left(4x,\\dfrac 1 4y\\right).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105681 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7861" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105681 #edb/ref 1071 "The point $(2,5)$ is stretched with invariant $y$-axis and stretch factor $2,$ and then stretched with invariant $x$-axis and stretch factor $-2.$ What is the resulting point?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105681 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "50e74298-c5c0-5bda-bb64-18778f156508" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105681 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's apply the given transformation.\n\n- A stretch of factor $2$ and invariant $y$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y) \\mapsto \\left(2x,y\\right).\n$$\n\n- A stretch of factor $-2$ and invariant $x$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y) \\mapsto \\left(x,-2y\\right).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the combination of the stretches is given by\n\n$$\n(x,y) \\mapsto \\left({\\color{blue}2}x,{\\color{red}-2}y\\right).\n$$\n\nApplying the combined stretch to our point, we obtain\n\n$$\n(2,5) \\mapsto \\left(2\\cdot 2, \\, -2\\cdot5 \\right) = (4,-10).\n$$\n\n![](images/0d/0d050ec1579f2ea2b37c01f2d7b60fd6580b6bc4766fcdd66005e1c2c103b8c7.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105842 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106350 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105842 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106532 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105842 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186534984 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105842 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186535019 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105842 #edb/ref 1039 "Applying a Combined Stretch to a Polygon" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105842 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186105679 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105842 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "7a4270f2-daf1-532d-804a-f293b6f1a8be" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105843 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049020 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105843 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106351 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105843 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106352 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105843 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186535009 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105843 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186535074 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105843 #edb/ref 1039 "Representing Combined Stretches Using Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105843 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186105680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105843 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "043fb5ef-143e-53cc-b83a-15df50446af4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105844 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106533 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105844 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106534 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105844 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186535028 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105844 #edb/ref 1039 "Applying a Combined Stretch to a Point" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105844 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186105681 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105844 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "28d37803-32d2-5b80-aa78-2f0d728e18fe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105996 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105996 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106801 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105996 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106802 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105996 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106803 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105996 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105996 #edb/ref 1045 "Combining Stretches of Geometric Figures" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105996 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186106800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105996 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050239 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105996 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105996 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "559742f9-a7fb-5d9d-b42f-6e5ba4ec6fe2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106534 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186105352 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106534 #edb/ref 1069 "q-88617" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106534 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106534 #edb/ref 1071 "The point $(4,2)$ is stretched with invariant $y$-axis and stretch factor $2,$ and then stretched with invariant $x$-axis and stretch factor $-3.$ What is the resulting point?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106534 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "20947e98-c606-5c7e-861f-e50700e68b13" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106534 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's apply the given transformation.\n\n- A stretch of factor $2$ and invariant $y$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(2x,y).\n$$\n\n- A stretch of factor $-3$ and invariant $x$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(x,-3y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the combination of the stretches is given by\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(2x,-3y).\n$$\n\nApplying the combined stretch to our point, we obtain\n\n$$\n(4,2)↦(2\\cdot 4,\\,-3\\cdot 2)=(8,-6).\n$$\n\n![](images/ab/ab3fda7652a99346f6d33e11b43d3401e2a427ab6d2f54c0f8717733fb3f892c.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106800 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106802 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106800 #edb/ref 1061 29237 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106800 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "86ae05de-9e43-5780-aadb-91a2390674a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106800 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186107117 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106801 #edb/ref 1061 29238 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106801 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d8a5d2be-6294-59cf-b218-a7ad2bfec89f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106801 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105842 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106802 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106803 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106802 #edb/ref 1061 29242 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106802 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1d1ebf4b-bb90-53a4-8143-fdfa9ab8c46c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106802 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105843 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106803 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106801 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106803 #edb/ref 1061 29247 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106803 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bc9e6b5d-f462-59ca-a575-27ec78d66323" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106803 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105844 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107117 #edb/ref 1064 "We can combine stretches in the $x$-direction (with invariant $y$-axis) and stretches in the $y$-direction (with invariant $x$-axis).\n\nFor example, let's consider a combined stretch transformation that performs stretches in the following sequence:\n\n- a stretch in the $x$-direction with stretch factor $\\dfrac{1}{2},$ followed by\n\n- a stretch in the $y$-direction with stretch factor $-\\dfrac{1}{2}.$\n\nThe functional representation of the combined stretch is given by\n\n$$\n(x,y) \\mapsto \\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}x, -\\dfrac{1}{2}y\\right).\n$$\n\nAs it turns out, it does not matter which stretch we perform first. But it's often helpful to think of the stretches being applied one at a time.\n\nLet's apply our combined stretch transformation to the polygon below.\n\n![](images/9b/9b0338a600efa76b14397a4d60b6de500daf4e136b2233b6fa4f021f0861fc24.png)\n\nTo stretch a polygon, we \n\n- find the images of the vertices, and then\n\n- draw segments connecting the image vertices.\n\nSo, our three vertices $(4,8)$, $(8,-4)$, $(-8,-8)$ are mapped to the following points by the stretch:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4,8) & ↦(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4,\\,-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8)=(2,-4) \\\\ (8,-4) & ↦(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8,\\,-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-4))=(4,2) \\\\ (-8,-8) & ↦(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-8),\\,-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-8))=(-4,4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following result:\n\n![](images/ec/ecc35921e58a7a307fe941825209e0009ff7a1bdb42fc252c2b7ef6db7876e75.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107117 #edb/ref 1065 4725 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107117 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "3c0d8bf1-1c0c-5e90-afed-61d70eaa5926" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107117 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534286 #edb/ref 1080 "images/36/36e66a86bca25711839b36dd2597d8b8b96c5a9c531c6fa77ee8a13dec831d41.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534286 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534286 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0b01cf01-6055-5206-8628-9df03691af89" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534304 #edb/ref 1080 "(x,y)↦(x,4y)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534304 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534304 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "127c4155-1f19-5cc4-9c19-a0d3041bb683" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534326 #edb/ref 1080 "(x,y)↦(4x,y)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534326 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534326 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1f295345-6a68-5dab-b6a6-eb286ab41b2c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534342 #edb/ref 1080 "(4,12)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534342 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534342 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "23bd6a64-92c7-5a5d-a870-0e7c3474eddb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534352 #edb/ref 1080 "(x,y)↦(3x,4y)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534352 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534352 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "29faaffe-98fa-5db1-917a-0be3d37da2a8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534357 #edb/ref 1080 "(x,y)↦(x,5y)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534357 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534357 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2e2598ef-553f-5520-951f-18966c644f5e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534364 #edb/ref 1080 "(x,y)↦(5x,2y)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534364 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534364 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3497c86f-9024-5137-b2c8-e6adf9725485" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534368 #edb/ref 1080 "(5,20)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534368 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592