n the $y$-direction can be represented by the following function:\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(3x,2y)\n$$\n\nTo stretch a polygon, we \n\n- find the images of the vertices, and then\n\n- draw segments connecting the image vertices.\n\nSo, our three vertices $(1,3)$, $(1,-2)$, $(-2,2)$ are mapped to the following points by the stretch:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1,3) & ↦(3\\cdot 1,2\\cdot 3)=(3,6) \\\\ (1,-2) & ↦(3\\cdot 1,2\\cdot (-2))=(3,-4) \\\\ (-2,2) & ↦(3\\cdot (-2),2\\cdot 2)=(-6,4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following result:\n\n![](images/6c/6c77ca7fa6efa27125c131c629b5afeba784b8ca4fd1039530879c2ec177b8dc.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535009 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186534969 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535009 #edb/ref 1069 "q-88610" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535009 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535009 #edb/ref 1071 "What function represents a stretch of factor $4$ and invariant $x$-axis, followed by a stretch of factor $3$ and invariant $y$-axis?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535009 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "501956c6-823d-5f9c-8694-d92497158079" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535009 #edb/ref 1074 "- A stretch of factor $4$ and invariant $x$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(x,4y).\n$$\n\n- A stretch of factor $3$ and invariant $y$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(3x,y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the combination of the stretches is given by\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(3x,4y).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535019 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186534851 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535019 #edb/ref 1069 "q-45450" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535019 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535019 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/76/7625ed8002bbd684ba004185f357e8b8e9b3384857684ef836ccd4a019a317cd.png)\n\nThe stretch $S(x,y)=(\\frac{1}{2}x,\\frac{1}{3}y)$ is applied to the polygon shown above. Which of the following is the resulting polygon?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535019 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "63c2d1f3-bff7-58f3-9c73-044cb81121d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535019 #edb/ref 1074 "To stretch a polygon, we \n\n- find the images of the vertices, and then\n\n- draw segments connecting the image vertices.\n\nSo, our three vertices $(4,6)$, $(5,-3)$, $(-6,-6)$ are mapped to the following points by the stretch:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4,6) & ↦(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4,\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 6)=(2,2) \\\\ (6,-3) & ↦(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6,\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-3))=(3,-1) \\\\ (-6,-6) & ↦(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-6),\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-6))=(-3,-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following result:\n\n![](images/aa/aa9f0b7c785c5c830c0e902f500fe0998df4c4ee8ace07af6989cf9aad2a88ea.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535028 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186534909 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535028 #edb/ref 1069 "q-88767" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535028 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535028 #edb/ref 1071 "The point $(5,-5)$ is stretched with invariant $y$-axis and stretch factor $2,$ and then stretched with invariant $x$-axis and stretch factor $2.$ What is the resulting point?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535028 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "758a989a-3043-5362-867a-7a0673f17cc3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535028 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's apply the given transformation.\n\n- A stretch of factor $2$ and invariant $y$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(2x,y).\n$$\n\n- A stretch of factor $2$ and invariant $x$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(x,2y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the combination of the stretches is given by\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(2x,2y).\n$$\n\nApplying the combined stretch to our point, we obtain\n\n$$\n(5,-5)↦(2\\cdot 5,\\,2\\cdot (-5))=(10,-10).\n$$\n\n![](images/8e/8e3eccf9b9190db3c19e2d49d633763d420947daa12929a8516fcf066465165d.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535074 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186534843 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535074 #edb/ref 1069 "q-88759" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535074 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535074 #edb/ref 1071 "What function represents a stretch of factor $5$ and invariant $x$-axis, followed by a stretch of factor $2$ and invariant $y$-axis?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535074 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "dd1b71b5-3284-5639-806c-2226f712ef21" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535074 #edb/ref 1074 "- A stretch of factor $5$ and invariant $x$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(x,5y).\n$$\n\n- A stretch of factor $2$ and invariant $y$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(2x,y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the combination of the stretches is given by\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(2x,5y).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
